# The lever-driven gate (Actionable Wall with movement=vertical; forest-0 x 2096, forest-1 x 480), one 48x96 frame drawn at
# the Wall's rect and following it as it rises (Wall.render). Replaces the generated orange brick pillar (wall-brick, #236
# art review, 2026-11-21); the author chose wood in the mechanism colours, like the lifts, over a first stone draft.
# A mechanism, so the active family and tier (D76), in the lift's palette (GreyOff.png / GreyOn.png: ink 211f30, steel
# 48475b / 62677a / 858d99, lit afbbc3, top d8e1e4): weathered grey planks, not the terrain's browns. Its lit top edge is
# the lift's (a d8e1e4 row under the moon rim the export adds, D92, RIM_OBJECTS). Five heavy vertical planks with grain (r, m)
# and knots (d), each lit on its right edge (h; the moon is up and to the right, D114), dark seams, and three darker iron
# bands with a light rivet on every plank. Exported by tools/export_object_sprites.py (export_gate_wall).
size 48 96
color K 211f30
color d 211f30
color r 48475b
color m 48475b
color a 62677a
color h 858d99
color w d8e1e4
color I 141320
color i 2e2d3c
color s afbbc3
frame wall
